  "title": "sport-lang course document",
  "description": "One way in to one event — a distance, a category — as a GeoJSON FeatureCollection whose rules travel in `sport:` members (SPEC.md §2.1, §2.2). This schema carries the per-field laws: `sport:version` a whole number from 1, longitude in [-180, 180] and latitude in [-90, 90], a LineString of at least two positions, every `along_m`, `from_m` and `to_m` on a feature or a path slice at least 0, and `repeat` at least 1. It cannot carry the cross-document laws, which need an engine: no feature id used twice, every segment and path slice ending after it starts, a path naming only lines the document carries, at least one line, no place beyond the end of the path, every point a rule names present, and a rule requiring an observation only at a place that produces it. Nor does it read a rule’s `params`, which belong to its dialect, or know which kinds need a place (`station_required`, `qualifies_within`). A document this schema accepts can still be refused to run. Members not named here are allowed and ignored, like GeoJSON foreign members. A version other than 1 is a document this specification does not run: an engine refuses it and still draws it (SPEC.md §7). Generated from ts/src/document.ts by ts/scripts/make-schema.ts; do not edit by hand.",
